    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The project's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and both its tests \u2014 the two new soft-delete acceptance tests \u2014 are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed owner deletion from a hard delete to a soft delete, keeping each piece of logic in its natural place:\n\n**1. `Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` field (mapped to a `deleted` column, defaulting to `false`) with a getter/setter, so a newly created owner is `deleted = false`.\n\n**2. Service** (`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`):\n- `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true` and saves, retaining the row instead of removing it.\n- Added a small `isActive(Owner)` helper capturing \"not soft-deleted.\"\n- The two create-time checks now skip soft-deleted owners via that helper: `rejectIdentityCollision` (identity check) and `findHouseholdMembers` (household-duplicate check). So a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been deleted.\n\n**3. OpenAPI spec** (`resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it through by name. `GET /api/owners/{id}` therefore returns `deleted` (false before delete, true after).\n\n**4. DB schemas** \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql). Tests run against HSQLDB, which requires `DEFAULT` before `NOT NULL`.\n\nThe controller's `DELETE` already returned 204 (a 2xx), so no change was needed there. Excluding soft-deleted owners from `findHouseholdMembers` also naturally keeps them out of the `householdSize`/`possibleDuplicate` computations, giving one coherent notion of an \"active\" household member.",
